Sync cc_op and EIP at every instruction boundary when a plugin is loaded

v/pstepper's plugin reads and writes the guest register file and redirects
execution with qemu_plugin_set_pc() from an arbitrary instruction boundary.
The i386 translator only materializes EIP and the lazily tracked condition
codes into env where it has a reason to, so at such a boundary they belong to
some earlier instruction -- EFLAGS read back through the register interface,
or recomputed by the guest after a redirect, comes from a stale cc_op with
fresh cc_src/cc_dst.

Without this, pstepper_signal_test, pstepper_xsave_test and
pstepper_ucontext_test segfault under an otherwise identical qemu; with it,
all five of v/pstepper's tests pass. It is not upstream, so CI has to apply
it: recovered from ~/src/External/QEMU on the development box, which is the
tree /opt/qemu was built from (its build directory's binary is byte-identical
to the installed one).

ci/build-qemu.rb applies every *.patch in this directory, in name order, with
`git apply` after checking out the pinned commit.

diff --git a/target/i386/tcg/translate.c b/target/i386/tcg/translate.c
index d8de290acb..1c32df7ab9 100644
--- a/target/i386/tcg/translate.c
+++ b/target/i386/tcg/translate.c
@@ -3483,6 +3483,29 @@ static void i386_tr_insn_start(DisasContextBase *dcbase, CPUState *cpu)
     DisasContext *dc = container_of(dcbase, DisasContext, base);
     target_ulong pc_arg = dc->base.pc_next;
 
+    /*
+     * A plugin callback can read and write the architectural register file
+     * (QEMU_PLUGIN_CB_R_REGS / _RW_REGS) and can redirect execution
+     * (qemu_plugin_set_pc()) from a point in the middle of a TB. EIP and the
+     * lazy condition-code state are materialized into env only where the
+     * translator has a reason to, so at an arbitrary instruction boundary
+     * they belong to some earlier instruction: EFLAGS read back through the
+     * register interface, or recomputed by the guest after such a callback
+     * redirected execution, would be derived from a stale cc_op with fresh
+     * cc_src/cc_dst. Sync both at every instruction boundary when a plugin
+     * is loaded -- two stores per instruction, and only then.
+     *
+     * This happens before prev_insn_end is taken on purpose. The ops belong
+     * to the state *entering* this instruction, which is exactly the state
+     * the TB must leave behind if disas_insn goes on to rewind this
+     * instruction (the tcg_remove_ops_after() path below); keeping them
+     * outside that range is what keeps cc_op_dirty honest afterwards.
+     */
+    if (unlikely(dcbase->plugin_enabled)) {
+        gen_update_cc_op(dc);
+        gen_update_eip_cur(dc);
+    }
+
     dc->prev_insn_start = dc->base.insn_start;
     dc->prev_insn_end = tcg_last_op();
     if (tb_cflags(dcbase->tb) & CF_PCREL) {
